{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01GdqSzQHWthdHCP7xoFyCRY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. This project derives specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI (mage-claude-orchestrator), and verifies parity through differential testing against Homebrew GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components:\n- `pkg/testutils/` — differential testing harness (compares Go vs GNU binary outputs)\n- `pkg/sys/` — Darwin/Linux syscall abstractions\n- `pkg/format/` — shared output formatting (tables, colors, human-readable sizes)\n- `cmd/` — one package per utility, compiled to standalone binaries\n\n**Current state**: All three `pkg/` libraries have implementation code on the working branch (`pkg/testutils/difftest.go`, `pkg/sys/stat.go+terminal.go`, `pkg/format/color.go+size.go+table.go`). No test files exist for any of them. No `cmd/` packages exist on the working branch. Specs are complete for releases 00.0 through 01.3.\n\n**Current release**: **00.0** (Batch 0 — foundational infrastructure) with four use cases:\n- uc001-magefiles (only `cmd/version` is a generation target; magefiles/ excluded by DD7)\n- uc002-format (implementation exists, no tests)\n- uc003-sys (implementation exists, no tests)\n- uc004-testutils (implementation exists, no tests)\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nAll three `pkg/` packages have implementations but no tests. Per P5 (dependency ordering), `pkg/testutils/` is the most foundational — every utility's differential tests depend on it working correctly. Testing the test harness first ensures the verification infrastructure is sound before building anything on top of it. This maps to **rel00.0-uc004-testutils**.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"prd001-testutils R2.1, R3.2-R3.5, R4.1-R4.4 -- pkg/testutils unit tests\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd001-testutils.yaml (requirements R2, R3, R4)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc004-testutils.yaml (use case for testutils)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-00.0.yaml (test cases for rel00.0 use cases)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (implementation under test)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/testutils/difftest_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Unit tests for RunDiffTests, divergence detection, normalization, and TimestampNormalizer\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Test RunDiffTests (prd001-testutils R2.1): verify that RunDiffTests executes both binaries with identical args, stdin, and env, and the subtest passes when stdout, stderr, and exit code all match\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Test divergence detection (prd001-testutils R3.2, R3.3, R3.4, R3.5): verify that RunDiffTests fails the subtest when stdout diverges, when stderr diverges, or when exit codes differ between the two binaries\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Test normalization (prd001-testutils R4.1, R4.3, R4.4): verify that NormalizeFunc hooks in DiffTest.Normalize are applied to both binaries' output before comparison, and that ComposeNormalizers applies functions in order\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Test TimestampNormalizer (prd001-testutils R4.2): verify replacement of 'Mon DD HH:MM:SS', 'YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS', and standalone 'HH:MM:SS' patterns with the '<TIMESTAMP>' placeholder\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Tests exercise only the public API exported by pkg/testutils: RunDiffTests, TimestampNormalizer, ComposeNormalizers. No modifications to difftest.go.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Use 'sh' with '-c' as the binary path for both goBinary and refBinary arguments, passing different echo commands to produce controlled stdout, stderr, and exit code. This avoids compiling fixture binaries while exercising the full fork-exec-capture path.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go test ./pkg/testutils/... passes with no failures\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"Tests cover matching outputs (pass case), divergent stdout, divergent stderr, and divergent exit code\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Tests cover single normalizer, ComposeNormalizers with two or more functions, and TimestampNormalizer with all three timestamp pattern variants from timestampPattern\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"difftest.go is unchanged -- all tests use the public API only\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":46346,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0abbbb04-f5d5-401a-9aee-e9a2cf80d9a9","uuid":"67ef8702-9a4c-4a57-97b4-abb43335ac17"}
